WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.460
Autolone delinquencies at 2010 highs could pressure consumer discretionary holdings in your TFSA. This is Modern Investing Techniques, Episode 205. Quick reminder, everything we discuss here is for education and entertainment. The practice investment of the day uses simulated trades with no real money. I'm not a licensed financial advisor and this isn't financial advice. Always do your own research before putting real money to work. The S&amp;P 500 closed at 7659.

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:41.240
down 1.1%. The NASDAQ composite closed at 26,140, down 2.1%. That composite is up 12.50% year-to-date,

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:47.220
and up 16.83% since the practice record began on March 16, 2026.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:56.120
The Toronto Stock Exchange composite, or TSX, closed at 36,177, up 0.1%.

00:00:56.120 --> 00:01:02.785
The NASDAQ 100's drop of more than 4% this week is its weakest stretch since June, and

00:01:02.785 --> 00:01:06.705
that slide helps shove money out of growth names and into defensive sectors.

00:01:07.325 --> 00:01:13.185
Meta reports this week and Microsoft reports after October 28, so digital advertising and

00:01:13.185 --> 00:01:14.965
cloud guidance are still on the tape.

00:01:15.585 --> 00:01:17.965
Yesterday, we were watching the Bank of Canada path.

00:01:18.525 --> 00:01:23.745
Today, the next decision still sits several weeks away, and futures price only modest odds

00:01:23.745 --> 00:01:28.745
of a near-term cut, while the Federal Reserve path keeps tugging on rate-sensitive Canadian

00:01:28.745 --> 00:01:29.385
holdings.

00:01:29.905 --> 00:01:35.225
Utilities drew buying on the TSX, and energy names posted intraday gains in the same

00:01:35.225 --> 00:01:35.725
rotation.

00:01:36.365 --> 00:01:39.665
One in five Americans is behind on at least one auto loan.

00:01:40.205 --> 00:01:46.725
The US auto loan book now totals $1.7 trillion, larger than credit card balances as a share

00:01:46.725 --> 00:01:49.965
of household debt, according to figures circulating on X.

00:01:49.965 --> 00:02:00.205
The average vehicle on US roads is a record of nearly 13 years old because elevated financing costs and tighter credit are pushing replacement purchases down the road.

00:02:00.645 --> 00:02:08.065
Think of that fleet as a parking lot that is not turning over. The cars stay put and the retailers who need that turnover feel it later.

00:02:08.065 --> 00:02:13.345
Sustained high delinquencies have historically come before slower consumer spending and weaker

00:02:13.345 --> 00:02:18.445
demand for discretionary goods, which is a headwind for retail and auto-related holdings.

00:02:18.925 --> 00:02:24.445
Inside a tax-free savings account, or TFSA, the practical check is the monthly New York

00:02:24.445 --> 00:02:29.265
Fed delinquency release, then a comparison against the sector weights of any U.S. exposed

00:02:29.265 --> 00:02:31.045
consumer names you already hold.

00:02:31.465 --> 00:02:36.805
If a name derives more than 20% of revenue from U.S. auto-financing, the briefing's rule

00:02:36.805 --> 00:02:41.205
is to cut the position size until that delinquency series shows consistent improvement.

00:02:41.905 --> 00:02:46.785
Financials tied to auto-lending and discretionary retailers carry more downside in that tape.

00:02:47.345 --> 00:02:51.925
Defensive utilities and staples have tended to hold up better in similar credit stress windows.

00:02:52.625 --> 00:02:56.925
The pattern usually gives a three to six-month lead before the weakness shows up in earnings,

00:02:57.405 --> 00:03:01.685
which is the window to shift toward stable rate-sensitive sectors such as utilities,

00:03:02.185 --> 00:03:04.325
rather than waiting for the retail print to break.

00:03:04.325 --> 00:03:11.369
Hydro-1 limited ticker H on the TSX is this week's simulated weekly hold, shares only

00:03:11.369 --> 00:03:14.029
no real money, five sessions from entry.

00:03:14.569 --> 00:03:16.149
The strategy family is valuation.

00:03:16.909 --> 00:03:22.249
Evaluation entry on defensive cash flows plus grid investment momentum, tagged evaluation

00:03:22.249 --> 00:03:24.149
discipline and macro rotation.

00:03:24.789 --> 00:03:29.529
When consumer credit is weakening, the screen we have been using is stable cash flows first,

00:03:29.529 --> 00:03:35.949
then a valuation plus momentum filter, and that pairing is why this name is on the pad instead of a retailer.

00:03:36.589 --> 00:03:43.089
Price action is showing bullish momentum above recent support, and volume is not yet confirmed above the 20-day average.

00:03:43.669 --> 00:03:53.709
Confidence is medium, defensive characteristics and grid spending are two aligned factors, and the volume filter is still pending, so this is not a high confidence three factor setup.

00:03:54.209 --> 00:03:58.609
You see a utility with the cash flow screen passing, and the volume filter is still dark.

00:03:58.609 --> 00:04:01.349
Do you size a full unit or a smaller one?

00:04:01.829 --> 00:04:06.169
The smaller unit is the call because unconfirmed momentum is where this book has been getting

00:04:06.169 --> 00:04:06.469
hurt.

00:04:06.989 --> 00:04:11.829
The stop loss sits 8% below entry, so the trade respects the moving average in validation,

00:04:12.369 --> 00:04:16.029
and the five session target is plus 2% to plus 5%.

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:19.389
Invalidation is the sentence to copy into your own notes.

00:04:19.849 --> 00:04:24.289
Any downgrade of the grid investment program or a break below the 50-day moving average

00:04:24.289 --> 00:04:28.469
on the daily chart kills the thesis before the money is supposed to sit there hoping.

00:04:28.469 --> 00:04:33.289
We simulate the entry and hold it through the week, then we grade it on Friday against

00:04:33.289 --> 00:04:34.969
the NASDAQ over the same window.

00:04:35.914 --> 00:04:39.294
The simulated book has no newly closed trade since the last review.

00:04:39.914 --> 00:04:44.254
The most recent practice investment has already been graded, and current holdings stay open

00:04:44.254 --> 00:04:45.714
until their scheduled evaluation.

00:04:46.554 --> 00:04:49.354
There is no new realized result to put on the board today.

00:04:50.034 --> 00:04:53.714
Hydra One will be judged after its five sessions, not on today's tape.

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:58.390
Yahoo Finance's earnings calendar is the free screen for a week like this.

00:04:58.390 --> 00:05:04.090
It filters upcoming reports by date, market cap and sector, and it highlights consensus

00:05:04.090 --> 00:05:08.670
estimates and historical beats, which is the field you read before a mega-cap print

00:05:08.670 --> 00:05:10.110
starts shoving flows around.

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:15.790
Canadian investors can set alerts for TSX names reporting the same week as US peers,

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:19.650
which is how you spot a rotation early instead of reading it in the close.

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:24.150
The free tier covers most of that, premium ads deeper analyst revisions.

00:05:24.770 --> 00:05:27.250
I have no financial relationship with Yahoo Finance.

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:33.399
Interactive Brokers option chains show live bid-ask spreads and open interest for covered

00:05:33.399 --> 00:05:36.339
call strikes on TSX or NYSE names.

00:05:36.799 --> 00:05:42.139
You can model the exact premium before you commit capital, which is useful inside a TFSA

00:05:42.139 --> 00:05:47.299
where tax drag is already low, and the chain also shows implied volatility percentiles

00:05:47.299 --> 00:05:51.819
so you can see whether those premiums sit in the upper quartile of the 52-week range.

00:05:52.399 --> 00:05:55.659
I have no financial relationship with interactive brokers either.

00:05:56.715 --> 00:06:03.435
Strathcona Resources, ticker SCR on the TSX, jumped 5.32% on buying and energy.

00:06:04.055 --> 00:06:08.515
Calcine's tape on that move says any new position should wait until volume holds above

00:06:08.515 --> 00:06:13.675
the 20-day average, because a single-day surge in a rotation does not confirm follow-through,

00:06:14.035 --> 00:06:17.755
even when other Canadian energy names have already lifted production guidance.

00:06:18.888 --> 00:06:23.728
Royal Bank renewed and expanded its multi-year commitment to young and indigenous entrepreneurs,

00:06:23.728 --> 00:06:25.728
blenders, blending loans with mentorship.

00:06:26.308 --> 00:06:31.288
CalCine Media notes the pledge mixes philanthropic funding with operating capital and extends

00:06:31.288 --> 00:06:36.088
a partnership that has already helped thousands of founders across Canada, which is a slow

00:06:36.088 --> 00:06:40.168
burn read on small business lending exposure, not a same-week trade.

00:06:40.648 --> 00:06:48.988
The simulated book at $1,000 per trade stands at 79 total trades, a 51% win rate, 40 wins,

00:06:48.988 --> 00:06:54.768
308 losses and 1 break even, with a cumulative loss of $95.67.

00:06:55.508 --> 00:07:02.228
Matched window alpha versus the NASDAQ is minus 49.4% across 28 rules-based trades.

00:07:02.748 --> 00:07:06.328
Average return per trade is minus 0.12%.

00:07:06.328 --> 00:07:09.288
The best is plus 20.11%.

00:07:09.288 --> 00:07:12.768
The worst is minus 27.14%.

00:07:12.768 --> 00:07:14.748
And the current streak is 3 losses.

00:07:14.748 --> 00:07:20.888
The AI screen is treating unconfirmed momentum as a size down input, not as a green light,

00:07:21.328 --> 00:07:24.088
and this remains a learning book, not a record to copy.

00:07:24.768 --> 00:07:30.588
Your utility satellite just ran from 10% of a TFSA to 14% after a defensive rally.

00:07:31.478 --> 00:07:37.978
The core is XEQT, one all-equity ticker that keeps global exposure cheap, and the satellite

00:07:37.978 --> 00:07:43.878
is a utility's focused exchange-traded fund, or ETF, sized at 10%, so you can express

00:07:43.878 --> 00:07:49.138
a theme like grid modernization, or preferred share income without rebuilding the whole account.

00:07:49.758 --> 00:07:54.678
When that satellite drifts more than 3 percentage points through its band, or when the calendar hits

00:07:54.678 --> 00:08:00.738
a quarterly check, you trim it back to 10. Inside registered accounts that trim keeps taxable events

00:08:00.738 --> 00:08:06.298
light, which matters because contribution room is already limited. In a non-registered account,

00:08:06.458 --> 00:08:11.518
the same drift threshold still applies, but you also have to observe the superficial loss rule

00:08:11.518 --> 00:08:15.178
on gains or losses inside the 30-day window around the trade.

00:08:15.558 --> 00:08:19.698
October income can sit on top of that equity core without blowing up the weights.

00:08:20.458 --> 00:08:27.018
Desjardin fixed income and preferred share ETFs, including ticker DCU on the TSX, are set

00:08:27.018 --> 00:08:30.418
to pay at month end for unit holders of record in late October.

00:08:30.998 --> 00:08:35.378
Put a recurring quarterly reminder on the calendar and compare current weights to the original

00:08:35.378 --> 00:08:38.158
targets, rather than chasing last week's move.

00:08:38.158 --> 00:08:43.258
The misconception is that every satellite is a forever holding. Once the original

00:08:43.258 --> 00:08:48.598
thesis expires, a specific phase of the rate cut cycle, for example, you sell it or fold

00:08:48.598 --> 00:08:55.151
it back into the core. Before we wrap, at the next session, pull up Hydro1, ticker H, note

00:08:55.151 --> 00:08:59.751
the distance from Fridays closed to the 50-day moving average, and set a price alert

00:08:59.751 --> 00:09:05.531
2% below that average. That's modern investing techniques for today. If you found this useful,

